1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,324
In the kingdom of Eldmoor,

2
00:00:02,364 --> 00:00:04,410
a crown was about to change hands.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,140
On the eve of the coronation,

4
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:09,646
King Aldric and Queen Mera

5
00:00:09,686 --> 00:00:11,268
feasted with their daughter,

6
00:00:11,308 --> 00:00:12,208
Princess Lyra.

7
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:12,891
In the corner,

8
00:00:12,931 --> 00:00:14,018
the King's quiet brother,

9
00:00:14,058 --> 00:00:15,590
Alisson, polished the royal crown.

10
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,009
And Chancellor Voss

11
00:00:17,049 --> 00:00:18,429
whispered in the shadows.

12
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,575
By morning, the crown was gone.

13
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,088
The King raged,

14
00:00:22,128 --> 00:00:24,500
Lyra wept, and Chancellor Voss declared

15
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,458
that a thief walked among them.

16
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:31,381
That evening, a hooded thief crept

17
00:00:31,421 --> 00:00:33,568
across the rooftops with a heavy sack.

18
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,021
Someone in a green

19
00:00:35,061 --> 00:00:36,476
cloak was following him.

20
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,926
When the thief looked away,

21
00:00:38,966 --> 00:00:40,010
the sack was gone.

22
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,506
Later that night,

23
00:00:42,546 --> 00:00:43,839
Lyra could not sleep.

24
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,036
From her balcony,

25
00:00:45,076 --> 00:00:47,251
she saw a lantern by the old vault,

26
00:00:47,291 --> 00:00:48,581
and Alisson, hiding a

27
00:00:48,621 --> 00:00:50,203
green bundle in the wall.

28
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,502
At the council,

29
00:00:54,542 --> 00:00:55,960
Voss revealed a clue:

30
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,001
a green thread,

31
00:00:57,041 --> 00:00:58,291
torn from a cloak.

32
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,785
Find Alisson, the King commanded.

33
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:02,678
But Alisson's chair stood empty.

34
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,408
The next night,

35
00:01:05,448 --> 00:01:07,406
Lyra crept to the wall herself.

36
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,564
Inside the bundle lay the crown,

37
00:01:09,604 --> 00:01:10,504
and a note.

38
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,774
Trust me. Watch Voss.

39
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:17,242
Alisson was not running away.

40
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:20,385
At dawn, he met Captain Bren in secret,

41
00:01:20,425 --> 00:01:21,420
gave him a note,

42
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:23,920
and pointed at the Chancellor's tower.

43
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,988
In his tower, Voss raged at the thief:

44
00:01:29,028 --> 00:01:30,292
the crown was lost.

45
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,591
But behind the curtain,

46
00:01:32,631 --> 00:01:34,497
Captain Bren heard every word.

47
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,417
At the coronation,

48
00:01:38,457 --> 00:01:39,689
the doors swung open.

49
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,728
Alisson carried in the true crown.

50
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,233
The hired thief confessed,

51
00:01:43,273 --> 00:01:44,646
and Voss was dragged away.

52
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:47,297
Alisson had protected the crown all along.

53
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,547
Lyra was crowned,

54
00:01:48,587 --> 00:01:50,329
and the whole kingdom cheered.

55
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,975
Queen Lyra ruled wisely.

56
00:01:54,015 --> 00:01:56,734
And quiet Alisson went back to polishing,

57
00:01:56,774 --> 00:01:57,784
just as before.

58
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,079
The end.

